# Normalise line endings in the working tree, store LF in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The Reference site is the specification and must stay byte-identical.
# No normalisation, no diffing — it is never edited, only read and screenshotted.
reference/** -text -diff

# The Pour Tracker is the co-founder's release, byte for byte (ticket 49): a
# changed copy calls itself unofficial. Its code is minified onto a few long
# lines, so a diff of it says nothing either. The copy kept with the code is
# the fallback (ADR-0024), held to its checksum file, so neither may be
# rewritten on the way into the repository.
src/pour-tracker/fallback/index.html -text -diff
src/pour-tracker/fallback/index.html.sha256 -text

# The test release is held to its own checksum, and has CRLF line endings on
# purpose, to catch a check that reads it as text (ticket 100).
tests/pour-tracker-test-release/** -text

# Binary assets
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
